# What `docker/Dockerfile`'s `COPY . .` must NOT drag into the build context.
#
# Both entries are about the same failure in two forms. A developer's tree carries target/ dirs from
# host builds; copying them in makes the context tens of megabytes and — worse — lets a stale
# artifact shadow what the builder stage compiles, so a green build can ship bytes nobody just
# produced. .git is the same cost with none of the benefit: nothing in the build reads history.
#
# This file is the CONTEXT ROOT's, so it applies to `--local context=.` builds of docker/Dockerfile
# and to nothing else. `docker/Dockerfile.musl-builder` is built with `docker/` as its context —
# qits-bootstrap-cli builds it that way too — and is unaffected.
target/
**/target/
.git/

# And the build's OWN outputs, which land here as `--output type=local,dest=out`. Without this line
# the release pipeline's second export (the SBOM stage) sends a context containing the binary the
# first one just wrote, `COPY . .` hashes differently, and the document costs a whole second native
# compile.
out/
